      "question": {
        ":question/id": "d918be29-c441-51f1-9f1b-f40474e59861",
        ":question/problem": "Expressed as a fraction in its simplest form, $\\log_{256}(64)$ equals{{field-1}}.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n\\log_a X=\\frac{\\log_b X}{\\log_b a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=256$ and $X=64.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ are powers of $2,$ we set $b=2.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{256}(64) &=\\frac{\\log_{2}(64)}{\\log_{2}(256)} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\log_{2}({2}^{6})}{\\log_{2}({2}^{8})} \\\\ &=\\frac{6}{8} \\\\ &=\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
